well new details in the officer-involved  shooting outside an elementary school  this morning  it happened in the southeast valley by  sandhill and twain  kristen drummond is live outside with  the latest details on this  kristin christian the shooting happened  before  nine this morning outside harris  elementary school here behind me  the campus was placed on a soft lockdown  which is normal  whenever there is police activity nearby  ccsd confirms that a ccsd police officer  was involved  in the shooting it happened when their  motorcycle unit was out here doing  enforcement  an officer pulled a driver over who  requested to speak to a supervisor  ccsd police say the supervisor was there  and approached the driver  at some point the driver decided to roll  up his window and drive away  knocking the supervisor to the ground  and causing his gun to go off  ccsd police say the shooting did not  seem though to  impact the school day it has absolutely  had no impact on education the kids  we've been inside the school several  times  kids have been going to and from class i  don't think most of the staff inside  don't even know what's going on out here  ccsd police are reviewing body camera  video and looking for the driver as well  as the car  which is a black nissan anyone with  information can call ccsd police the  numbers at the bottom of your screen at  or metro 702-799-5411 who are also  helping with the investigation  now ccsd police say the supervisor who  was knocked over was looked at  and is fine and they also suspect that  the driver  is well and is fine as well now this is  the  first officer involved shooting for the  department in about  five years reporting live in the east  valley kristen drummond 8 news now
 

